-do" aria-hidden=3D"true" class=3D"anchor" id=3D"user-content-what-to-do"><=
/a>What to do</h2>
<p data-sourcepos=3D"8:1-9:199" dir=3D"auto">The purpose of this module is =
to get knowledge about CloudFormation and prepare a CloudFormation template=
 (YAML or JSON based) with the whole AWS architecture you will need to comp=
lete future modules.
After that all resources will be handled by CloudFormation and you will be =
able to easily delete the resources when you don't need them and create at =
any time. Such automation could save your budget.</p>
<p data-sourcepos=3D"11:1-11:99" dir=3D"auto">In the next modules you will =
be able to scale your CloudFormation template by adding new resources.</p>
<p data-sourcepos=3D"13:1-13:87" dir=3D"auto">The AWS architecture that sho=
uld be implemented with Cloud Formation template is below:</p>
<p data-sourcepos=3D"15:1-15:37" dir=3D"auto"><a class=3D"no-attachment-ico=
n gfm" href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-associate-training/=
-/raw/master/courses/CloudX_Associate_AWS_Developer/tasks/cf/images/cf-app-=
infrastructure.png" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank"><img data=
-sourcepos=3D"15:1-15:37" src=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-a=
ssociate-training/-/raw/master/courses/CloudX_Associate_AWS_Developer/tasks=
/cf/images/cf-app-infrastructure.png" alt=3D"" decoding=3D"async" class=3D"=
gfm js-lazy-loaded" loading=3D"lazy" data-testid=3D"js-lazy-loaded-content"=
></a></p>
<h3 data-sourcepos=3D"17:1-17:52" dir=3D"auto">
<a href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-associate-training/-/bl=
