k-1--create-a-cloud-formation-template" aria-hidden=3D"true" class=3D"ancho=
r" id=3D"user-content-sub-task-1--create-a-cloud-formation-template"></a>Su=
b-task 1 =E2=80=93 Create a Cloud Formation template</h3>
<p data-sourcepos=3D"19:1-19:300" dir=3D"auto"><em data-sourcepos=3D"19:1-1=
9:300">Please note that all the resources that you need to add have already=
 been created by you in the previous modules, and now you need to transfer =
their settings to the template. You can create template manually or use <a =
data-sourcepos=3D"19:217-19:298" href=3D"https://console.aws.amazon.com/clo=
udformation/designer" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer noopener" target=3D"_blank=
">Cloud Formation Designer</a>.</em></p>
<ol data-sourcepos=3D"21:1-83:0" dir=3D"auto">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"21:1-25:35">Add a S3 bucket:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"22:4-25:35">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"22:4-22:41">Use <em data-sourcepos=3D"22:10-22:26">AW=
S::S3::Bucket</em> resource type.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"23:4-23:51">The name doesn't include uppercase charac=
ters.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"24:4-24:38">The name includes your full name.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"25:4-25:35">The name begins with a letter.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"26:1-53:169">Add a VPC:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"27:4-53:169">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"27:4-27:39">Use <em data-sourcepos=3D"27:10-27:24">AW=
S::EC2::VPC</em> resource type.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"28:4-28:179">The name should follow this convention <=
em data-sourcepos=3D"28:45-28:69">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-Network</em> (note th=
at the name is set using keypair tag and this requirement does not apply to=
 the resource Logical ID).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"29:4-29:44">The CIDR block should be <em data-sourcep=
os=3D"29:31-29:43">10.0.0.0/16</em>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"30:4-33:119">Add an InternetGateway in the VPC:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"31:7-33:119">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"31:7-31:40">Use <em data-sourcepos=3D"31:13-31:39">AW=
S::EC2::InternetGateway</em>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"32:7-32:190">The name should follow this convention <=
em data-sourcepos=3D"32:48-32:80">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-InternetGateway</em> =
(note that the name is set using keypair tag and this requirement does not =
apply to the resource Logical ID).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"33:7-33:119">Attach <em data-sourcepos=3D"33:16-33:42=
">AWS::EC2::InternetGateway</em> to the <em data-sourcepos=3D"33:51-33:75">=
&lt;ProjectName&gt;-Network</em> VPC using <em data-sourcepos=3D"33:87-33:1=
18">AWS::EC2::VPCGatewayAttachment</em>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"34:4-39:85">Add a Public Subnet A in the VPC:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"35:7-39:85">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"35:7-35:45">Use <em data-sourcepos=3D"35:13-35:30">AW=
S::EC2::Subnet</em> resource type.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"36:7-36:189">The name should follow this convention <=
em data-sourcepos=3D"36:48-36:79">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubnet-A</em> (=
note that the name is set using keypair tag and this requirement does not a=
pply to the resource Logical ID).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"37:7-37:48">The CIDR block should be <em data-sourcep=
os=3D"37:34-37:47">10.0.11.0/24</em>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"38:7-38:179">Availability zone should be set up using=
 <em data-sourcepos=3D"38:50-38:178"><a data-sourcepos=3D"38:51-38:177" hre=
f=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/intrins=
ic-function-reference-getavailabilityzones.html" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer=
 noopener" target=3D"_blank">GetAZs</a></em>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"39:7-39:85">Assign <em data-sourcepos=3D"39:16-39:47"=
>&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubnet-A</em> to the <em data-sourcepos=3D"39:56=
-39:80">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-Network</em> VPC.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"40:4-45:85">Add a Public Subnet B in the VPC:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"41:7-45:85">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"41:7-41:45">Use <em data-sourcepos=3D"41:13-41:30">AW=
S::EC2::Subnet</em> resource type.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"42:7-42:189">The name should follow this convention <=
em data-sourcepos=3D"42:48-42:79">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubnet-B</em> (=
note that the name is set using keypair tag and this requirement does not a=
pply to the resource Logical ID).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"43:7-43:48">The CIDR block should be <em data-sourcep=
os=3D"43:34-43:47">10.0.12.0/24</em>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"44:7-44:179">Availability zone should be set up using=
 <em data-sourcepos=3D"44:50-44:178"><a data-sourcepos=3D"44:51-44:177" hre=
f=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/intrins=
ic-function-reference-getavailabilityzones.html" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer=
 noopener" target=3D"_blank">GetAZs</a></em>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"45:7-45:85">Assign <em data-sourcepos=3D"45:16-45:47"=
>&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubnet-B</em> to the <em data-sourcepos=3D"45:56=
-45:80">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-Network</em> VPC.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"46:4-53:169">Set up public routing:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"47:7-53:169">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"47:7-47:53">Add route table using <em data-sourcepos=
=3D"47:31-47:52">AWS::EC2::RouteTable</em>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"48:7-48:183">The name should follow this convention <=
em data-sourcepos=3D"48:48-48:73">-RouteTable</em> (note that the name is s=
et using keypair tag and this requirement does not apply to the resource Lo=
gical ID).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"49:7-49:85">Assign <em data-sourcepos=3D"49:16-49:47"=
>-PublicRouteTable</em> to the <em data-sourcepos=3D"49:56-49:80">&lt;Proje=
ctName&gt;-Network</em> VPC.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"50:7-50:101">Add route using <em data-sourcepos=3D"50=
:25-50:41">AWS::EC2::Route</em> (note that route should be created after in=
ternet gateway).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"51:7-51:98">Assign <em data-sourcepos=3D"51:16-51:41"=
>-RouteTable</em> and <em data-sourcepos=3D"51:47-51:79">&lt;ProjectName&gt=
;-InternetGateway</em> for created route.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"52:7-52:56">Set up destination CIDR block for created=
 route.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"53:7-53:169">Add subnet associations with route table=
 for <em data-sourcepos=3D"53:54-53:85">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubnet-A<=
/em> and <em data-sourcepos=3D"53:91-53:122">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubn=
et-B</em> using <em data-sourcepos=3D"53:130-53:168">AWS::EC2::SubnetRouteT=
ableAssociation</em>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"54:1-83:0">Add a Linux-based EC2 instance:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"55:4-83:0">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"55:4-61:193">Add and configure a security group so th=
at:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"56:6-61:193">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"56:6-56:51">Use <em data-sourcepos=3D"56:12-56:36">AW=
S::EC2::SecurityGroup</em> resource type.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"57:6-57:181">The name should follow this convention <=
em data-sourcepos=3D"57:47-57:70">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-SecGr1</em>. (note th=
at the name is set using keypair tag and this requirement does not apply to=
 the resource Logical ID).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"58:6-58:76">Assign <em data-sourcepos=3D"58:15-58:38"=
>&lt;ProjectName&gt;-SecGr1</em> to the <em data-sourcepos=3D"58:47-58:71">=
&lt;ProjectName&gt;-Network</em> VPC.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"59:6-59:123">It allows access over HTTP/HTTPS from an=
ywhere (better use <em data-sourcepos=3D"59:67-59:98">AWS::EC2::SecurityGro=
upIngress</em> resource type for that).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"60:6-60:59">It allows SSH connections from your IP ad=
dress only.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"61:6-61:193">Note: If you plan to deploy the applicat=
ion to some other port, then you need to add one more <em data-sourcepos=3D=
"61:102-61:133">AWS::EC2::SecurityGroupIngress</em> resource type for that =
port. (Ex. TCP 8080 for backend app)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"62:4-70:79">Add launch template for EC2:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"63:6-70:79">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"63:6-63:52">Use <em data-sourcepos=3D"63:12-63:37">AW=
S::EC2::LaunchTemplate</em> resource type.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"64:6-64:189">The name should follow this convention <=
em data-sourcepos=3D"64:47-64:78">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-LaunchTemplate</em>. =
(note that the name is set using keypair tag and this requirement does not =
apply to the resource Logical ID).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"65:6-65:281">Add parameter for AMI (use custom AMI wi=
th your application that was created in <a data-sourcepos=3D"65:88-65:110" =
href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-associate-training/-/blob/=
master/courses/CloudX_Associate_AWS_Developer/tasks/ec2/README.md" class=3D=
"gfm">EC2</a> module). More info about Cloud Formation parameters can be fo=
und <a data-sourcepos=3D"65:177-65:280" href=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com=
/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/parameters-section-structure.html" rel=
=3D"nofollow noreferrer noopener" target=3D"_blank">here</a>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"66:6-66:78">The parameter name should follow this con=
vention <em data-sourcepos=3D"66:57-66:77">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-AMI</em>.</l=
i>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"67:6-67:69">Set up the instance AMI using <em data-so=
urcepos=3D"67:38-67:58">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-AMI</em> parameter.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"68:6-68:231">Add parameter for instance type (use fre=
e-tier instance type). More info about Cloud Formation parameters can be fo=
und <a data-sourcepos=3D"68:127-68:230" href=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com=
/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/parameters-section-structure.html" rel=
=3D"nofollow noreferrer noopener" target=3D"_blank">here</a>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"69:6-69:87">The parameter name should follow this con=
vention <em data-sourcepos=3D"69:57-69:86">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-InstanceType=
</em>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"70:6-70:79">Set up the instance type using <em data-s=
ourcepos=3D"70:39-70:68">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-InstanceType</em> parameter.</=
li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"71:4-76:49">Add an auto-scaling group:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"72:6-76:49">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"72:6-72:62">Use <em data-sourcepos=3D"72:12-72:47">AW=
S::AutoScaling::AutoScalingGroup</em> resource type.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"73:6-73:190">The name should follow this convention <=
em data-sourcepos=3D"73:47-73:80">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-AutoScalingGroup</em>=
 (note that the name is set using keypair tag and this requirement does not=
 apply to the resource Logical ID).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"74:6-74:93">Assign <em data-sourcepos=3D"74:15-74:46"=
>&lt;ProjectName&gt;-LaunchTemplate</em> to the <em data-sourcepos=3D"74:55=
-74:88">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-AutoScalingGroup</em> ASG.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"75:6-75:92">Assign <em data-sourcepos=3D"75:15-75:46"=
>&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubnet-A</em> and <em data-sourcepos=3D"75:52-75=
:83">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubnet-B</em> subnets.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"76:6-76:49">Scale out when CPU usage is more than 50%=
.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"77:4-83:0">Add an application load balancer to the au=
to-scaling group:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"78:6-83:0">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"78:6-78:69">Use <em data-sourcepos=3D"78:12-78:54">AW=
S::ElasticLoadBalancingV2::LoadBalancer</em> resource type.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"79:6-79:186">The name should follow this convention <=
em data-sourcepos=3D"79:47-79:76">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-LoadBalancer</em> (no=
te that the name is set using keypair tag and this requirement does not app=
ly to the resource Logical ID).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"80:6-80:92">Assign <em data-sourcepos=3D"80:15-80:46"=
>&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubnet-A</em> and <em data-sourcepos=3D"80:52-80=
:83">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-PublicSubnet-B</em> subnets.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"81:6-81:73">Set up ALB listener using <em data-source=
